\begin{definition}\cite{gv}
A fuzzy-valued function $f:[a,b]\to E^1$ is called Riemann integrable on $[a,b]$, if there exists $I\in E^1$ with the property : $\forall\varepsilon>0$, $\exists\delta>0$ such that for any division of $[a,b]$ $d : a=x_0<x_1<\cdots<x_n=b$ of norm $v(d)<\delta$, and for any points $\xi_i\in[x_i,x_{i+1}]\ i=\overline{0,n-1}$, we have $$D\left(\sum\limits_{i=0}^{n-1}f(\xi_i)(x_{i+1}-x_i), I\right)<\varepsilon.$$ Then $I=\int\limits_a^bf(x)dx$.
